        "problem": "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x=6 \\\\ -3x+4y=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $4$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $6$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $4$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ |  |  |  |  |",
        "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
